      <div purpose="faq-section">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <div purpose="accordion">
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-1" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-1" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-1">
              Do I need Autopilot to use Fleet?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-1" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-1">
              <p>No. Autopilot is a bundling strategy. It requires Entra, and it’s how Microsoft gets you paying for Entra and Intune.</p>
              <p>With Fleet, zero-touch setup is simpler. Fleet gives you an order email. Forward it to Dell, Lenovo, or HP, and they install Fleet before the device ships. That’s it. Every new PC arrives already managed by Fleet.</p>
              <p>Veeva runs thousands of Windows PCs with Fleet and no Autopilot.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-2" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-2" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-2">
              What Microsoft license does zero-touch setup need?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-2" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-2">
              <p>None. Just forward the email from Fleet to Dell, Lenovo, or HP.</p>
              <p>Autopilot is part of Microsoft’s bundling strategy to maximize revenue. If you already have Entra and want to keep it, Fleet fully supports Autopilot. But it isn’t required, and it isn’t how most of Fleet’s large enterprise customers set up new PCs.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-3" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-3" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-3">
              Intune is included in Microsoft 365 E3 and E5. Why pay for Fleet?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-3" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-3">
              <p>Because you’ll save money. For example, switching from Microsoft 365 E3 to Office 365 E3 saves about $13 per user per month. That’s almost double the price of Fleet.</p>
              <p>Even if you have no plans to change your Microsoft licenses, or another team owns that decision, you still save money and gain flexibility. Choose the identity provider and EDR you want for your Windows PCs, without paying for a subscription you don’t want or need. And stop maintaining Entra and Intune just to make the bundle work.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-4" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-4" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-4">
              Can I use Fleet in a hybrid Active Directory environment?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-4" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-4">
              <p>Yes. Fleet works with Active Directory, Entra, or both, including hybrid-joined PCs. Fleet customers run it on thousands of Windows PCs in mixed environments.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-5" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-5" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-5">
              Can I migrate from Intune without wiping devices?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-5" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-5">
              <p>Yes. Fleet’s automatic Windows MDM migration moves hosts from Intune or another MDM to Fleet without wiping them and without the end user having to do anything.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-6" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-6" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-6">
              Which versions of Windows does Fleet support?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-6" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-6">
              <p>Windows 10 and 11 get full MDM, including enrollment, profiles, BitLocker, software, and OS updates. Windows Server gets visibility, vulnerability reporting, and scripts.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-7" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-7" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-7">
              Does Fleet support Windows on ARM?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-7" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-7">
              <p>Yes. Fleet’s agent runs natively on Windows ARM64 devices, such as Snapdragon-based Copilot+ PCs. Fleet-maintained apps include ARM64 builds where vendors publish them.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="accordion-item">
            <p purpose="accordion-header" id="accordion__header-faq-8" class="accordion" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#accordion__body-faq-8" aria-controls="accordion__body-faq-8">
              How does Fleet keep Fleet-maintained apps safe?
              <span class="fa fa-angle-down"></span>
            </p>
            <div purpose="accordion-answer" id="accordion__body-faq-8" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="accordion__header-faq-8">
              <p>Installers come straight from the vendor and are verified against a pinned SHA-256 hash. Every catalog change is installed and uninstalled on real hosts and reviewed by a person before release, and any version that fails testing is held back.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p purpose="faq-note">Want to see it for yourself? <a href="/contact?talkToUs">Book a meeting</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>

